---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Customer Success & Customer Operations" current="/customer-success/" description="Richard Allen's experience in customer success, customer experience, SaaS support, technical support, training, people management, customer journeys, and customer operations.">
<section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Customer Success & Customer Operations</div><h1>Customer relationships backed by strong operating discipline.</h1><p class="lede">My customer-facing work combines relationship management, SaaS and technical support, people leadership, training, escalation management, customer feedback, reporting, and the operating discipline needed to make service clearer and more consistent.</p></div></section>

<section class="section impact-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="stats-grid compact-stats">
    <article class="stat-card teal"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">6 yrs</span></div><div class="metric-label">in HawkSoft customer and technical support</div></article>
    <article class="stat-card blue"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">32</span></div><div class="metric-label">Customer Support and Technical Support representatives managed after promotion to Customer Support Manager</div></article>
    <article class="stat-card gold"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">1+ yr</span></div><div class="metric-label">co-leading cross-functional Customer Journey work across the customer lifecycle</div></article>
    <article class="stat-card violet"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">2</span></div><div class="metric-label">customer-facing technology organizations with SaaS/support experience</div></article>
  </div>

  <div class="experience-path" aria-label="Customer experience lifecycle">
    <div class="path-step"><span>01</span><strong>Understand</strong><small>Listen to customers and identify friction</small></div>
    <div class="path-line"></div>
    <div class="path-step"><span>02</span><strong>Support</strong><small>Troubleshoot, escalate, and keep work moving</small></div>
    <div class="path-line"></div>
    <div class="path-step"><span>03</span><strong>Enable</strong><small>Train customers and staff on better workflows</small></div>
    <div class="path-line"></div>
    <div class="path-step"><span>04</span><strong>Improve</strong><small>Feed patterns back into process and product work</small></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Customer-facing proof</div><h2>Where service, systems, and operations meet.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Selected examples from HawkSoft, The Kotter Group, and related customer-operations work.</p></div>
  <div class="grid two value-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">TEAM</div><h3>Support management & coaching</h3><p>Promoted from Team Lead to Customer Support Manager at HawkSoft and managed 32 Customer Support and Technical Support representatives. Work included hiring and disciplinary authority, performance management, workflow coverage, escalations, quality review, stand-ups, and one-on-one coaching.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">SaaS</div><h3>Technical support & adoption</h3><p>Supported insurance-agency customers using HawkSoft CMS, trained customers and staff on software features and workflows, handled complex escalations, and coordinated customer database and hosted-service transitions.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">CX</div><h3>Customer Journey leadership</h3><p>Co-led a cross-functional Customer Journey / Customer Lifeline initiative for about a year with approximately 26 participants, mapping customer touchpoints across the relationship and helping teams identify handoffs, friction, and retention opportunities beyond their own departments.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">BUILD</div><h3>Building a Customer Experience function</h3><p>At The Kotter Group, established and managed a Customer Experience / Customer Success function, maintained relationships across the client base, gathered feedback, resolved issues, and supported service improvement and retention.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">LEARN</div><h3>Training & customer education</h3><p>Created training documentation, presentations, webinars, online content, and customer communications at The Kotter Group, while HawkSoft work included customer and staff training on troubleshooting, workflows, product changes, and best practices.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">DATA</div><h3>Service reporting & pattern recognition</h3><p>Built operational and management reporting from support and call data, turning large Excel exports into information leadership could use for staffing, training, procedure, policy, and service decisions.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section tight"><div class="container"><div class="callout"><strong>Best-fit customer-facing roles:</strong> customer operations, customer success leadership, enablement, onboarding, implementation support, service operations, training, and customer-experience work where the focus is improving the system—not personally carrying a high-volume phone queue.</div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/case-studies/">See case studies</a><a class="button secondary" href="/resume/">View résumé</a><a class="button secondary" href="/contact/">Contact</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
